# BATCH PROCESSING NOTES #

[this is a description of the current implementation rather than a set of instructions.]

I've now transformed hundreds of files of all sizes from MARC 2 RDA, using snippets of script on both windows and linux. These transformations were largely experimental in nature, often testing a single aspect of the MARC2RDA code or the GraphDB repository configuration. The results of these tests might be conveyed in informal emails, assembled into excel spreadsheets on occasion, etc. But a common report for encapsulating this processing was lacking, which meant that any knowledge gleaned from these tests was unlikely to persist. 

The first step was to determine what data should be collected during this processing. (Ideally this data should be provided by the MARC2RDA transformation, but as yet, no metrics whatsoever are provided by that script). What information would be useful? The file names and sizes (marc inputs, RDF outputs, error logs) and the count of items in each; the version of the transformation code used; the time it took to run the transformation; the repository into which the transformed data was loaded, and the time it took for that process.

Eventually this basic form took shape:

