Scan the MARC file for UTF-8 problems.
A single encoding error will crash the transform. Therefore, 'runt' should have access to a tool that can identify and neutralize these errors before the transform begins. I do have the beginnings of a script that will identify these errors, but it does not 'fix' them. Unfortunately, the most well-known tool for this task--iconv--stops on the first error it finds.

Scan the RDF results for IRI problems.
A single corrupt IRI will crash GraphDb's import process. Therefore, 'runt' should have access to a tool that can identify and neutralize these errors before the import begins. I do have the beginnings of a script that will identify these errors, but it does not 'fix' them. Unfortunately, the most well-known tool for this task--apache jena riot--stops on the first error it finds.

